{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_0199eaixFDsFZAEzTVp5z1Zu", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_Moreau_Gottschalk\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.classicals.de/gottschalk\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.taminoautographs.com/blogs/autograph-blog/louis-moreau-gottschalk-the-first-great-american-composer\"}, {\"url\": \"https://phoenixcd.com/artist_conductor/louis-moreau-gottschalk/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://classicalm.com/en/composer/282/--\"}, {\"url\": \"https://sin80.com/en/artist/gottschalk\"}, {\"url\": \"https://pt.billiongraves.com/grave/Louis-Moreau-Gottschalk/5785341\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.bellperc.com/blogs/repertoire/louis-moreau-gottschalk\"}, {\"url\": \"https://loebjewishportraits.com/biography/louis-moreau-gottschalk/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://wikipedia.classicistranieri.com/en/articles/l/o/u/Louis_Moreau_Gottschalk_afc5.html\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:41:32.664Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Louis Moreau Gottschalk collapsed yellow fever performance Rio de Janeiro theater", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01F72aLRjnYJn8ettH6i7qu2", "content": [{"title": "Louis Moreau Gottschalk", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_Moreau_Gottschalk"}, {"title": "www.classicals.de", "url": "https://www.classicals.de/gottschalk"}, {"title": "Louis Moreau Gottschalk - The First Great American Composer December 24 2020", "url": "https://www.taminoautographs.com/blogs/autograph-blog/louis-moreau-gottschalk-the-first-great-american-composer"}, {"title": "Louis Moreau Gottschalk", "url": "https://phoenixcd.com/artist_conductor/louis-moreau-gottschalk/"}, {"title": "Louis Moreau Gottschalk", "url": "https://classicalm.com/en/composer/282/--"}, {"title": "sin80.com", "url": "https://sin80.com/en/artist/gottschalk"}, {"title": "pt.billiongraves.com", "url": "https://pt.billiongraves.com/grave/Louis-Moreau-Gottschalk/5785341"}, {"title": "louis moreau gottschalk", "url": "https://www.bellperc.com/blogs/repertoire/louis-moreau-gottschalk"}, {"title": "Louis Moreau Gottschalk", "url": "https://loebjewishportraits.com/biography/louis-moreau-gottschalk/"}, {"title": "Louis Moreau Gottschalk afc5", "url": "https://wikipedia.classicistranieri.com/en/articles/l/o/u/Louis_Moreau_Gottschalk_afc5.html"}]}, "Sources agree that Gottschalk collapsed during a concert at the Teatro Lyrico Fluminense in Rio de Janeiro on November 24, 1869, and died three weeks later. They disagree on the illness and the exact date.\n\n- **Collapse and illness:** Most sources say he collapsed from yellow fever. One Wikipedia-derived page says it was malaria, and Gottschalk contracted malaria in Brazil in August 1869, which suggests the earlier infection may have been malaria. One account gives November 25 and says he collapsed at the keyboard.\n- **Last piece:** He had just finished playing his romantic piece Morte! (translated from Portuguese as \"Death\"), although the actual collapse occurred just as he started to play his celebrated piece Tremolo.\n- **Death:** He died on December 18, 1869, at his hotel in Tijuca. The cause is disputed. Some sources say probably from an overdose of quinine, while others say there is some debate as to whether he died from an overdose of quinine, or from sepsis from empyema. One alternative cause is appendicitis, which led to peritonitis.\n- **Burial:** In 1870, his remains were returned to the United States and were interred at the Green-Wood Cemetery in Brooklyn, New York."], "durationSeconds": 5.811580333, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_0199eaixFDsFZAEzTVp5z1Zu", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
